# Default Compose profiles for the full dev stack (docker-compose.yml).
#
# Compose profiles are opt-in, so each backend sits behind a profile and the default pair
# is selected here. Plain `docker compose up` brings up Garage and OpenBao alongside the
# always-on service; the other backends are not created, started or pulled.
#
# To switch a backend, override this whole variable on the command line. Do not also pass
# a `--profile` flag: when both are set, their precedence varies by Compose version, so a
# backend you meant to drop can stay active. Select backends through COMPOSE_PROFILES only.
#
#   # minio instead of Garage. minio is deprecated for new deployments but still supported
#   # as an external endpoint. Point the node at it via the S3 endpoint and region overlay:
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=minio,openbao GDI_S3_ENDPOINT=http://minio:9000 GDI_S3_REGION=us-east-1 docker compose up -d --build
#
#   # HashiCorp Vault instead of OpenBao. Vault is a fully supported alternative, not
#   # deprecated. Point the node at it and tell the init one-shot which seal flow to drive:
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=garage,vault VAULT_ADDR=http://vault:8200 SECRETS_BACKEND=vault docker compose up -d --build
#
#   Both secrets profiles use file storage, so the node identity and the Transit key
#   survive restarts. OpenBao auto-unseals via a static seal. Vault keeps a stored 1-of-1
#   Shamir key and comes back sealed after a restart until secrets-init replays it, which
#   is why SECRETS_BACKEND must be set for that profile. `scripts/dev-reset.sh --yes`
#   wipes secrets and data together.
#
#   # Both alternatives at once. SECRETS_BACKEND is required by the vault profile: without
#   # it, secrets-init drives the OpenBao seal flow against Vault, no unseal key is stored,
#   # and the stack comes back sealed after a restart.
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=minio,vault GDI_S3_ENDPOINT=http://minio:9000 GDI_S3_REGION=us-east-1 VAULT_ADDR=http://vault:8200 SECRETS_BACKEND=vault docker compose up -d --build
#
#   Ceph RADOS Gateway is a supported deployment backend with no local Compose service.
#   Point a node at an external RGW endpoint with docker-compose.external.yml instead. Do
#   not pass `COMPOSE_PROFILES=ceph`: Compose does not warn on an unknown profile, so the
#   stack would come up with no S3 backend while the node dialled a host that does not
#   resolve.
#
# The one-shot secrets-provisioning container runs separately and enables its own profile:
#   docker compose run --rm setup
COMPOSE_PROFILES=garage,openbao
